  "term": "Kleine–Levin syndrome",
  "definition": "Kleine–Levin syndrome is a rare disorder marked by repeated episodes of extreme sleepiness, often with increased eating, confusion, restlessness, and sometimes hallucinations. The episodes usually last days to weeks, can recur several times a year, occur mainly in males in adolescence or early adulthood, and may go away on their own over several years.",
